<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Karel Čapek</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1890">1890</a>–<a href="/years/1938">1938</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Karel Čapek was a Czech writer and journalist of the interwar republic and a friend of President Masaryk. His play R.U.R. of 1920 introduced the word robot, coined by his brother Josef, and his novel War with the Newts satirised fascism and greed. A leading democrat, he died in December 1938, soon after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/munich-agreement">Munich Agreement</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/karel-capek.jpg" alt="Karel Čapek" width="210" height="299" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Karel-capek.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
